<article class="env-lemma" id="08BT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08BT">Lemma <span data-tag="08BT">20.32.8</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ be a ringed space. Let $U \subset X$ be an open subset. Denote $j : (U, \mathcal{O}_ U) \to (X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ the corresponding open immersion. The restriction functor $D(\mathcal{O}_ X) \to D(\mathcal{O}_ U)$ is a right adjoint to extension by zero $j_! : D(\mathcal{O}_ U) \to D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows formally from the fact that $j_!$ and $j^*$ are adjoint and exact (and hence $Lj_! = j_!$ and $Rj^* = j^*$ exist), see Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/09T5" data-tag="09T5">13.30.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>